rmRingView\n- When nil, skip audio playback (just show the UI)\n- HomeView passes nil (or we could pick first alarm)\n- For the visual test from HomeView, pass an alarm if available\n\nActually, I think the simplest approach that satisfies the Day 4 brief is to add an optional `alarm: Alarm?` parameter where if nil, we skip audio playback. This is a shell that will later be wired up to real notification delivery.\n\nSo I'll make AlarmRingView accept an optional alarm parameter, and in HomeView I can pass the first available alarm from the query for testing purposes. Then I need to create the RewardView with a wheat gold background, a congratulatory message with an emoji, and the Totoro avatar.\n\nFor the RewardView, I'll use the dismiss environment variable to auto-dismiss after 3 seconds. The AlarmRingView will present the RewardView as a full-screen cover when the user completes the alarm action. Then I need to update the AlarmScheduler to use the alarm's sound file name instead of the default system sound.\n\nI'm also thinking about the validate.sh script - I need to add a check that lists all Swift files in the SunnyWalker directory and verifies they're included in the Xcode project.\n\npbxproj file, failing with a clear error if any are missing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2116,"cache_read_input_tokens":46642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2116,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":30,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fbe470b3-8eb0-4896-9f42-f0cc667bfcff","uuid":"2d372d80-296c-4781-a85e-c4c848931e06","request_id":"req_011CbaK1MZUd5HxfEktrX2KR"}
